cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use harmonizer in your work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "harmonizer: signal-checked channel harmonisation for sleep recordings"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Purcell
    given-names: Lorcan
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-11-16
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Lorcan7274/harmonizer"
abstract: >-
  Checks what each channel of a sleep recording (EDF) really is against what its header claims,
  maps channels to standard names, and writes Luna CANONICAL rules, MNE channel types,
  BIDS channels.tsv, stager channel picks and a review page for the channels that need a reader.
keywords:
  - sleep
  - polysomnography
  - EDF
  - harmonisation
  - Luna
